<content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>Use the following passage to answer questions 1–3.</para>
<para>In a newly formed swamp, it is estimated that there are 500 mosquitoes. The population is estimated to double each day.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Let \(m\) represent the total population of mosquitoes and \(d\) represent the number of days that have passed since the first estimate. What is the equation that represents the growth of the mosquito population?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      \(m=d\cdot 500^2\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(m=2\cdot 500^d\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(m=500\cdot 2^d\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(m=500\cdot d^2\)
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(m=500\cdot 2^d\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What does \(d=-2\) represent in this context?</item></list>
  <list>
    
    <item>
      This represents 2 days before the first estimate was taken.
    </item>
    <item>
      This represents the day before the first estimate was taken.
    </item>
    <item>
      This represents the day the first estimate was taken.
    </item>
    <item>
      This represents 2 days after the first estimate was taken.
    </item>
  </list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> This represents 2 days before the first estimate was taken.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the estimated number of mosquitoes that were in the new swamp 1 day before the estimate was taken?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      500
    </item>
    <item>
      250
    </item>
    <item>
      1,000
    </item>
    <item>
      125
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 250</para>
<para>Use the following passage to answer questions 4–6.</para>
<para>A desert pond is slowly drying up. The average volume of the pond is shown in the table. The first year it was measured, the average volume was determined to be 40,000 liters. Double click on mathematical expression/equation to enlarge.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <table>
    <tgroup cols="2"><thead>
      <row>
        <entry>\(y\), years</entry>
        <entry>\(v\), volume (liters)</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
          –4
        </entry>
        <entry> </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
        –2
        </entry>
        <entry> </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          0
        </entry>
        <entry>
          40,000
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          1
        </entry>
        <entry>
          20,000
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          3
        </entry>
        <entry>
          5,000
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </tgroup></table>
  <item> Which equation represents the pond’s water loss?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      \(y=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^v\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(v=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^y\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(v=20,000\cdot\left(\frac14\right)^y\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(v=\frac12\cdot\left(40,000\right)^y\)
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(v=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^y\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> What does \(y=-2\) represent in this context?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>the time it took for the pond to shrink by a factor of 2
    </item>
    <item>the first time the volume was measured
    </item>
    <item>the time 2 years after the first time the volume was measured
    </item>
    <item>the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> What was the average volume of the pond 4 years before the first time the volume was measured?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      320,000 liters
    </item>
    <item>
      160,000 liters
    </item>
    <item>
      80,000 liters
    </item>
    <item>
      640,000 liters
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 640,000 liters</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which of the following is equivalent to 6,350,000 in scientific notation?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      \(6.35\times 10^4\)</item>
    <item>
      \(6.35\times 10^5\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(6.35\times 10^6\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(6.35\times 10^7\)
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(6.35\times 10^6\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which of the following is equivalent to 0.00032 in scientific notation?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      \(3.2\times 10^{-3}\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(3.2\times 10^{-4}\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(3.2\times 10^{-5}\)
    </item>
    <item>
      \(3.2\times 10^{-6}\)
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(3.2\times 10^{-4}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which of the following is equivalent to \(7.24\times 10^3\) in decimal form?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      7,240
    </item>
    <item>
      724
    </item>
    <item>
      72,400
    </item>
    <item>
      724,000
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 7,240</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following is equivalent to \(5.47\times 10^{-5}\) in decimal form?</item></list>
  <list>
    <item>
      0.00547
    </item>
    <item>
      0.0000547
    </item>
    <item>
      0.00000547
    </item>
    <item>
      0.000547
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0.0000547</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which of the following correctly orders these values from greatest to least?</item>
  <table>
    <tgroup cols="2"><thead/>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>Value R</entry>
        <entry>
         0.00161
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
          <entry>Value S</entry>
        <entry>
         \(6.35\times 10^{-3}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>Value T</entry>
        <entry>
          0.000541
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>Value U</entry>
        <entry>
         \(7.23\times 10^{-4}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </tgroup></table>
</list>
  <list>
    <item>
      Value S, Value R, Value T, Value U
    </item>
    <item>
      Value R, Value S, Value T, Value U
    </item>
    <item>
      Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T
    </item>
    <item>
      Value R, Value S, Value U, Value T
    </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T</para>
</section>
</content>
